oe was a Korean politician and soldier during the Joseon period.", "newValue": "Han Myŏnghoe (1415–1487) emerged as a preeminent political strategist and military commander during Korea's Joseon Dynasty, profoundly shaping the mid-15th century's power landscape. Born in Seoul on November 26, 1415, he rose from a relatively obscure background to become a central figure in the tumultuous politics of the early Joseon era, particularly as a key architect of the 1453 coup d'état that elevated Prince Suyang (later King Sejo) to the throne. His influence persisted through several reigns, fundamentally altering the trajectory of the Joseon court and its internal political dynamics for decades.

